# Changes to these paths need an approval from a member of
# @archestra-ai/engineering other than the author. They decide what CI runs
# with release secrets and cloud credentials, so one compromised account must
# not be able to change them alone. Everything else merges without review.
#
# The "code-owner-review" ruleset enforces this (archestra-ai/infra,
# github/org). Team membership lives there too (github/org/teams.tf).
#
# Keep the list short: every path here needs a second person on each PR that
# touches it.
# Release Please's manifest, version file and the changelogs are not owned, so
# release PRs stay self-merge.

/.github/workflows/                                 @archestra-ai/engineering
/.github/actions/                                   @archestra-ai/engineering
# Scripts the workflows run, including the archestra updater's App-key step.
/.github/scripts/                                   @archestra-ai/engineering
# Pinned tools CI installs and runs.
/.github/tools/                                     @archestra-ai/engineering
/.github/release-please/release-please-config.json  @archestra-ai/engineering
/.github/dependabot.yml                             @archestra-ai/engineering
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                 @archestra-ai/engineering
